Realize the startup sprite cursor on every screen.

The root cursor is allocated before input devices exist, so the usual
RealizeCursorAllScreens pass cannot realize it. InitializeSprite later
realizes it only on the initial screen. FreeCursor nevertheless cleans
it up on every screen, and pointer movement can display it elsewhere.
In Xnest, both cleanup and display can dereference a NULL cursor-private
pointer on a secondary screen where the cursor was never realized.

Complete startup initialization at the point established by this
upstream fix:
https://github.com/XQuartz/xorg-server/commit/6ab311c92d036dc63ee92ab4bb231f5f61ebe69f

Upstream report:
https://github.com/XQuartz/XQuartz/issues/518

--- a/dix/events.c
+++ b/dix/events.c
@@ -3418,7 +3418,16 @@
     pSprite->current = pCursor;

     if (pScreen) {
-        (*pScreen->RealizeCursor) (pDev, pScreen, pSprite->current);
+        /*
+         * Prepare the cursor on every screen it may visit, then configure
+         * the sprite on its initial screen below.
+         */
+        for (int i = 0; i < screenInfo.numScreens; i++) {
+            ScreenPtr cursorScreen = screenInfo.screens[i];
+
+            (*cursorScreen->RealizeCursor) (pDev, cursorScreen,
+                                           pSprite->current);
+        }
         (*pScreen->CursorLimits) (pDev, pScreen, pSprite->current,
                                   &pSprite->hotLimits, &pSprite->physLimits);
         pSprite->confined = FALSE;
